Ark is a very nice survival game.
I had my doubts before buying because of the bad reviews, so I will make my review simpler.
Pros:
- Great survival game with Dinos;
- Grinding like all survival game;
- Dinos aren't easy to kill or avoid when you are starting;
- Crafting is pretty easy and that's a good thing compared to games without recipes to craft stuff;
- Graphics are gorgeous;
- Options when setting up your game are very good;
- Modes of game:
- You can Join Servers on PvP and PvE;
- Single Player Hosting
- Host your own Multiplayer game with friends, with password or without
- Both base and DLC maps are huge and I didn't scrached 10% of it;
Cons:
- OPTIMIZATION S HORROBLE, COMPLETELY♥♥♥♥♥♥
- I get 30 fps mixing with the graphics and getting a decent looking on my Geforce 965M 4GB
- But these nice FPS moments aren't durable. They vary and I can't say what is the cause, apart from the game using a huge ammount of RAM;
- Has a DLC while in Early Access;
- When launched I would like better optimization because my PC can handle better graphics but they don't seem optimized;
- Taming is a pain in the♥♥♥♥♥if you leave it on default. I use the speed on 3x faster;
- Dinos kill you early game with so much ease that can be annoying to some, not for me though;
- Dinos could have a much better AI;
Overall the game is good but the bad optmization that makes me run the game in ♥♥♥♥♥♥ graphics on my TOP PC isn't funny.

